WALKTHROUGHS, FINDINGS AND REVISIONS
=========================================

1. TASK PROMPTS
---------------
Task 1: "You're driving to Halifax this weekend. Find out how much the
         gas will cost."
Task 2: "You drive to work every day. Set up your own car in FuelFare and
         check what your commute costs."


2. METHOD
---------
Scenario-based walkthrough (no participant). Each task was
traced through the sitemap and the mobile, tablet and desktop wireframes.


3. OBSERVATIONS
---------------
Task 1 - Calculate a trip
- Expected path: Home calculator > Trip Results. Path works.
- Hesitation: the vehicle dropdown has no way to add a car if none is
  saved. Add Vehicle can only be reached from My Garage.
- Missed content: on mobile and tablet, Trip Results shows the gas price
  but not when it was updated.
- Confusion: "Current Vehicle" on Trip Results looks like a label, not a
  button to change the car.

Task 2 - Set up a car and check a commute
- Expected path: Account > Sign In > My Garage > Add Vehicle > Saved
  Trips > Trip Results.
- Viewport obstacle: the Home frames have no Account link at any size.
- Viewport obstacle: mobile Add Vehicle has no Engine / trim field, so
  mobile users may get the wrong fuel economy.


